00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the maple trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.590
Silver-White Alms

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.210
<i>Fall passes quickly in the Alps.</i>

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>Little by little, the days turn colder
as winter approaches.</i>

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:37.920
Come.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.820
Welcome back, Peter!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.080
I'm back.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.510
Welcome back!
It's cold, isn't it?

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.160
Yes, it is!

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.490
My nose is frozen.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.590
It's true! It's red!

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.720
It's not funny!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.400
It's so cold!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.460
It's snowing!

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.020
Snow! Snow!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.500
That's why it's so cold!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.630
Grandfather! Grandfather!

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.140
Grandfather, quickly!
Come with me!

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.060
Why are you yelling so much?

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.570
Come with me! Hurry! Hurry!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.360
Grandfather, snow!
It's snowing!

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.440
It's finally started.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.480
Look!

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.490
It's so beautiful!

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:08.140
They look like pieces of stars.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.110
It's falling! It's falling!

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.640
Keep falling! Keep falling!

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:17.020
Decorate everything in pure white!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.050
It's snow.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.410
It is so cold.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:24.620
How beautiful!

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.580
<i>Heidi, are you awake?</i>

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.100
Good morning, grandfather!

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:49.050
Look, isn't it beautiful? Yesterday, I slept
in a bed of soft and fluffy snow.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.530
I have to do something to prevent this.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.980
Heidi, what are you doing?

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.980
I'm trying to hear
if the fir trees still speak.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.860
And do they?

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.840
I don't know.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.310
At first, it seems like they make sounds.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.160
Then, it seems they don't make sounds.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.260
Grandfather, come here and listen with me.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.230
All right, all right.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.490
Let's see.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.390
So, can you hear it?

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.250
I don't know.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.080
At first, it seems like they make sounds.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.490
Then, it seems they don't make sounds.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.980
Grandfather, you sounded just like me!

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.740
Yes, I did.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.920
Joseph, come!

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.600
Oh, Joseph...

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:18.190
Grandfather!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.560
You scared me!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.540
Come here, Joseph!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.830
Hey, wait!

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.320
Joseph, wait!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.540
Joseph!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.360
Wait!

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.640
Hey, Joseph!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.230
It's cold!

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:13.900
Heidi, you're going to catch a cold!
Come inside quickly!

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.740
But Peter and the goats
haven't come yet!

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.860
Peter is not coming.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.990
Is Peter really not coming?

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.660
No. He doesn't go to the pastures
when there's snow.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.350
He won't come until spring.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.620
Then I won't see Peter, Snowflake
and the others until then?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.490
Well, no.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.890
What a pity.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.480
Grandfather, a deer!

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.150
Grandfather, come here a second!

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.470
What is it, Heidi?

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.560
There's a deer under the fir!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:35.970
Really?

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:37.640
Let me see.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.930
Hurry.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.250
See?

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.250
Yes.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:50.110
It's been standing there for a while.
I wonder if it is wounded?

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:55.350
It is hidden under the storm tree to
protect himself from the snow.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.240
What's a storm tree?

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:03.560
It's a tree that the animals normally
use to protect themselves, like that deer.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:08.200
Look, the branches of the tree extend
out that almost looks like a house.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.340
It's true. The snow does not enter.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:17.070
There is only snow around it.
What is it eating?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.250
I wonder if it's hungry.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:21.250
It must be.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.530
Then we have to give it something to eat.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.400
Yes.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:28.630
Go get a bit of hay. It will like it.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:29.630
Yes.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:45.150
Welcome, Mr. deer.
I have brought you a treat.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.950
What's wrong, Heidi?

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:01.890
It ran away.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:05.330
I wanted to be friends with it.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:10.520
Heidi. It is not possible to
become friends with it so quickly.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.900
It takes patience to create
a friendship with animals.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:18.900
Put the hay under the tree and wait.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:19.920
Yes.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.430
I did what you said, Grandfather.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:38.740
Grandfather, look.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.570
It is eating. It is eating it.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.410
<i>Winter in the Alps is very harsh.</i>

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:25.880
<i>But little Heidi barely notices,
for she has found a new delight.</i>

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:13.340
Here.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:45.860
Grandfather!

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:50.080
Grandfather, the deer already
eats from my hands!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.940
Really? I'm glad.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.660
He ate it! He ate it!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.520
Grandfather, look!

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:24.120
It looks like a deer!

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.830
Let me see.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.150
It looks like a deer, doesn't it?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.670
Grandfather, what are you doing?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.410
You'll see.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.070
It's a deer!

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.550
Are you sure?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.310
It's not a deer?

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:06.060
I know! It's a lord with big horns!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.390
That's right. It's an ibex.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.500
Thank you.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.820
What's wrong, Heidi?

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:47.000
The lord with big horns that you made,
made me miss Snowflake and the others.

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:23.630
I wonder how Snowflake and the others are doing?

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.330
Do not worry. They are fine as always.

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:35.800
That's true. I will see them all in spring.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:55.940
Grandfather, I think
there's someone outside.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:59.420
I heard something in the door.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:06.180
It's your imagination.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:10.300
There's no way someone
would come here in this storm.

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.110
Well, that's true.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.000
Like I thought, there's someone there.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:24.100
Maybe it's the snow man that
came here to eat you.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.070
You can't scare me.

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:46.370
Well, well! Look who it is!

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:53.720
Peter!

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:57.260
Peter, I'm so glad you're here!

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.130
Your hands are so cold!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.690
Come, get closer to the fire.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.500
Are you warm?

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.600
You'll be better after you eat.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:23.590
Well, eat.

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:24.890
Thank you for the food!

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.520
- Thank you for the food!

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:47.500
Peter, what do you do in the village?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:51.690
Huh? School is...

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:58.170
Since the Goat General has no
followers anymore, he has to turn to his pen.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.070
What? Turn to his pen?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.490
During the winter he must go to school.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:04.730
School?

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:05.630
Yes.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:08.620
Peter, what is a school?

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:15.190
Well, Peter?

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:16.810
The school is...

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:18.820
What do you see there?

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:20.830
Well...

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:22.920
What kind of people are there?

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.390
A horrible teacher!

00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:28.070
A teacher? What is that?

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.190
Well, a teacher is...

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:34.690
Well...

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:41.430
<i>Peter is very bad at expressing
his thoughts in words.</i>

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.240
<i>It's difficult for him to explain.</i>

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:49.220
<i>Still, he tries to describe what school is.</i>

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:52.240
<i>Studying is difficult and tedious.</i>

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:56.070
<i>Being with the goats is much more fun.</i>

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:58.990
<i>The teacher always scolds him,</i>

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:02.190
<i>and his schoolmates laugh at him.</i>

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:06.410
<i>He keeps talking about life in the school.</i>

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.200
Oh, Peter...

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.020
It's not funny.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.410
As you can see, Peter doesn't
find it very funny.

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:32.410
School seems a strange place.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:36.620
Thank you for the food.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.090
I've never eaten anything so delicious before.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.450
You don't need to say that,
because I won't give you more.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:47.030
I'm not a glutton!

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:07.600
Peter, I had a great day.

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:12.110
Go ahead and close your eyes

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:12.110
Itteoide me wo tojite

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:08.930
Me, too.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:11.440
Can I come back the next Sunday?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.120
Of course!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:17.830
Into the dream, the way of the dream

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:17.830
Yume no naka he yume no michi he

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.850
Right, Grandfather?

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.850
Right, Grandfather?

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:15.620
Yes.

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.760
Be careful on the way home.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.030
Thank you.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:22.850
Good night, cute goats

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:22.850
Kawaii yagi mo oyasumi

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:21.470
I'm going!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.010
in the pen,

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.010
Koya no naka

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:27.030
Goodbye!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.500
Good night, echoes

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.500
Kodama mo oyasumi

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:29.650
Goodbye!

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:33.950
in the valleys,

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:33.950
Tani no oku de

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:42.550
Good night! Good night!

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:42.550
Oyasumi oyasumi

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:42.550
Oyasumi oyasumi

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:42.680
Heidi, my grandmother really wants
you to come by someday.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:46.680
Will you come soon?

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:52.020
<i>Heidi has never thought she might</i>

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:55.030
<i>get an invitation to come
visit someone before now.</i>

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.940
<i>She's far too surprised to say anything.</i>

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:04.730
What's wrong, Heidi?

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:11.480
Peter, does your grandmother
really want to see me?

00:22:20.090 --> 00:22:21.200
Will you come?

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:22.820
Of course!

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:23.830
Then...

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:43.690
To think that someone wants
me to visit them. It's like a dream.

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:51.370
Grandfather.

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:54.810
Can I go tomorrow?

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.770
What's wrong, Grandfather?

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.040
Won't you let me go?

00:23:05.750 --> 00:23:11.440
No. It's been snowing a lot this winter,
and it's too dangerous to go out.

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:14.050
Well, then I can go when it's sunny, right?

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.510
I hope it will stop snowing soon.

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:27.970
<i>Grandfather uses the snow
as an excuse to Heidi.</i>

00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:31.590
<i>In reality, he doesn't want
Heidi to associate</i>

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.870
<i>with the people of the village.</i>

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:40.050
<i>Will he let Heidi go when it stops snowing?</i>

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:58.820
<i>A snowstorm is covering Alm Mountain in snow.</i>

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:02.950
<i>Heidi has decided to
visit Peter's grandmother,</i>

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:05.500
<i>but she isn't able to go outside at all.</i>

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:08.960
<i>One day, the storm finally clears up,</i>

00:24:09.180 --> 00:24:13.160
<i>and Heidi takes grandfather's sleigh
and visits Peter's house.</i>

00:24:13.420 --> 00:24:18.450
<i>Waiting in the house,
is the old, blind grandmother.</i>

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:21.800
<i>However, Heidi doesn't let that bother her,</i>

00:24:21.800 --> 00:24:26.300
<i>and spends a pleasant day on the mountain.</i>

00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:29.440
<i>Next episode:
To Grandmother's House</i>

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:31.440
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

